# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Course 3 ---
# Produced by a command in a c3-unitNN/README.md, and machine-specific, so the
# `git add c3-*` that first commits Course 3 must not sweep them in.
# `target/` (incl. c3-unit06's target/team-repo) is covered at the top of this
# file; `.m2-demo/` and `.m2-unit06/` by c3-unit02/.gitignore + c3-unit06/.gitignore.
# Scoped to their units, like the c2-unit24 block above, and kept here even
# where a per-unit .gitignore repeats them: same second net as Course 2.

# c3-unit01 README cmd 1: help:effective-pom -Doutput=effective-pom.xml
c3-unit01/effective-pom.xml

# c3-unit03 README cmd 5: dependency:build-classpath -Dmdep.outputFile=cp-$s.txt
# (absolute paths into whichever local repository resolved the jars)
c3-unit03/scopes/cp-*.txt

# c3-unit06 README cmd 1: help:effective-settings -Doutput=es.xml
# (its own README: "the file's header comment names your user and host")
c3-unit06/es.xml

# --------------------------------------------- Course 3 · Section 2 (Gradle) ---
# Everything below is produced by a command in a c3-unit07..10 README (or by that
# unit's receipts.sh). Scoped per unit, exactly like the Course 2 and Course 3
# blocks above, because `build/` is a plausible source directory name and a bare
# `build/` here would hide one in some future unit.
#
# NOT ignored, and deliberately committed: gradlew, gradlew.bat,
# gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar, gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties,
# mvnw, mvnw.cmd and .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties. The wrapper being in
# the repository IS the lesson of unit 10 - a .gitignore that swallowed it would
# contradict the unit it belongs to.

# Gradle's per-project state: the incremental-build database and the file hashes
# behind every UP-TO-DATE in unit 08.
c3-unit07/.gradle/
c3-unit08/.gradle/
c3-unit09/.gradle/
c3-unit10/.gradle/
c3-unit07/exercise/.gradle/
c3-unit08/exercise/.gradle/
c3-unit09/exercise/.gradle/
c3-unit10/exercise/.gradle/
c3-unit08/breaks/undeclared-input/.gradle/
c3-unit09/conflict/.gradle/

# GRADLE_USER_HOME="$PWD/.gradle-home" - line 3 of every README in this section.
# Holds the downloaded 9.7.1 distribution (~130 MB), the dependency cache, the
# build cache and the daemon registry. Deleting it leaves nothing of this course
# on the machine; it must never be committed.
c3-unit07/.gradle-home/
c3-unit08/.gradle-home/
c3-unit09/.gradle-home/
c3-unit10/.gradle-home/

# Throw-away Gradle homes: unit 10's sha256 demo and its older-distribution break,
# and the same demo in unit 10's exercise.
c3-unit10/.gh-fresh/
c3-unit10/.gh-old/
c3-unit10/exercise/.gh-fresh/

# Gradle's output directory. `target/` is already covered at the top of this file;
# this is its Gradle twin, and it also holds build/generated/menu (unit 08's
# generated MenuCatalog.java) and build/libs/lib (unit 10's five runtime jars).
c3-unit07/build/
c3-unit08/build/
c3-unit09/build/
c3-unit10/build/
c3-unit09/tiffinbox-core/build/
c3-unit09/tiffinbox-web/build/
c3-unit10/tiffinbox-core/build/
c3-unit10/tiffinbox-web/build/
c3-unit07/exercise/build/
c3-unit08/exercise/build/
c3-unit09/exercise/build/
c3-unit09/exercise/tiffinbox-core/build/
c3-unit09/exercise/tiffinbox-web/build/
c3-unit10/exercise/build/
c3-unit08/breaks/undeclared-input/build/
c3-unit09/conflict/build/

# -Dmaven.repo.local="$PWD/.m2-demo" - the isolated local repository every Maven
# command in this section uses so that ~/.m2 is never the subject. In unit 10 it
# also holds the Maven distribution ./mvnw downloads under MAVEN_USER_HOME.
c3-unit07/.m2-demo/
c3-unit09/conflict/.m2-demo/
c3-unit10/.m2-demo/

# Not ignored on purpose: c3-unit08/src/main/menu/menu.txt and
# c3-unit08/breaks/undeclared-input/src/main/menu/menu.txt. Both are committed with
# THREE lines. The README and receipts.sh append a fourth and put it back; if a run
# is interrupted, `git diff` on those two files is what tells you, which is the
# whole reason they are tracked.
